From: GKI maintainers <gki-builder@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] modules: report builtin zram providers as already loaded

OEM first-stage and system module lists can still request zram.ko and
zsmalloc.ko when both drivers are built into a replacement GKI. Loading
them would duplicate the providers or fail symbol resolution. Return
-EEXIST, which Android libmodprobe treats as an already-loaded success.

Only these exact names with their corresponding builtin config qualify.
Explicit module blacklists, signature/security checks, and version checks
for every module that actually loads retain their upstream behavior.

diff --git a/kernel/module.c b/kernel/module.c
--- a/kernel/module.c
+++ b/kernel/module.c
@@ -4079,6 +4079,16 @@
 		goto free_copy;
 	}
 
+	/* OEM module lists still include these drivers when our replacement
+	 * is built in. Use the normal already-loaded result; never load a
+	 * second implementation or relax version checks for other modules.
+	 */
+	if ((IS_BUILTIN(CONFIG_ZRAM) && !strcmp(info->name, "zram")) ||
+	    (IS_BUILTIN(CONFIG_ZSMALLOC) && !strcmp(info->name, "zsmalloc"))) {
+		err = -EEXIST;
+		goto free_copy;
+	}
+
 	err = rewrite_section_headers(info, flags);
 	if (err)
 		goto free_copy;
